 "structural_change": "RTL-BUILD-S81 (owner 0dv 10-18): NEW link-port leaf of the end-slice master (dsdv_slice_lepw/_e = ot_s81sl_slice + this leaf + 2 x dsfd_coll_lane): outward ring-port pin flops, per-lane 512-flit SRAM landing FIFOs (2 x 5 ot_sram_1r1w_512x128, as the coll lane's own replay/receive arrays), RX pair re-assembly, fault collector. Fills residual row 1 (lt_lk 8 x 512 undriven). Host plane (coordinator 10-18): seq_host f_host 515 / f_lf 4 / f_ks 53 out, t_host 77 / t_kd 54 in, as typed non-ring link frames (HOST / KS in, THOST / TKD out). Gate 3eb62a102 FAIL (GPL-0305 divergence): macro columns fronted the W/E pin faces (W band 15 um) with a 0.4-um sliver between the columns' halos and W/E pins at 99% face demand (5.9/um). Re-floorplan: 475.2 square (W/E 4.85/um), two 5-SRAM columns centred with a 21.6-um channel, >=31-um W/E std-cell bands, 119-um N/S bands. S81-RTLB3 (10-18, gate b6bf54dea WARNs): core-side lane faces become CREDIT links (lane LCR = 1, as the die's collective lanes): lo0_r / lo1_r land in one pin flop each (credit pulse; was 556 / 558 loads, 6 levels), RX landing DR 8 with registered one-hot slot enables and 16 replicated read pointers, li_r a registered credit pulse; rst_n -> ot_rst_relay 4 regions (was one flop, 1,232 loads), ri data bits unreset. Edges: ro -> lane endpoint +2, lane -> ri +1, reset release +1.",
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Source-registered (RTL-BUILD-S81): ro lands in pin flops (rov/roq), ri / lo_v / lo_d / li_r / rxv / fault leave flops, li handshake + data land in hq / dq flops, sl_f / l*_f land in slq / lfq; recipe pin_regs would add an unpriced stage."
 },
